web-presets-mode-mirror = Mirror: also remove the router's own settings in these groups that are not among these
web-presets-wireguard = WireGuard keys
web-presets-wireguard-regenerate = Make a new private key on the router for each tunnel
web-presets-wireguard-help = The report lists each new public key; register it on the VPN server.
web-presets-wireguard-shared = Clear this only to keep the captured key: two routers with one key break the tunnel on both while both connect.
web-presets-renames = Names on the router
web-presets-renames-text = Each interface and policy the settings name keeps its name unless you type another; the settings follow the new name.
web-presets-rename-interfaces = Interfaces
web-presets-rename-policies = Policies
web-presets-rename-source = In the settings
web-presets-rename-target = On the router
web-presets-rename-none = These settings name no interface and no policy.
web-presets-review-title = Review each setting
web-presets-review-text = What happens to each setting on the router and why. Clear Apply to leave a setting out; choices are saved as you make them.
web-presets-review-number = No.
web-presets-review-include = Apply
web-presets-fate-send = Sent
web-presets-fate-present = Already there
web-presets-fate-remove = Removed
web-presets-reason-add = kcc sends this setting to the router.
web-presets-reason-renamed = kcc sends this setting with the names you chose.
web-presets-reason-present = The router already has this setting; kcc sends nothing.
web-presets-reason-mirror = Mirror removes this setting of the router: these groups cover it and the settings lack it.
web-presets-reason-unsupported = The router's firmware cannot take this setting, so kcc leaves it out.
web-presets-reason-password = The password of { $name } is bound to the source's realm: type it in the inputs step, or leave the user out.
web-presets-reason-mapping = The settings name { $name }, which needs a name on the router: set it in the options step, or leave the setting out.
web-presets-reason-conflict = The router's value differs and needs a decision: leave the setting out to keep the router's value.
web-presets-reason-wireguard-new = The router makes a new private key for this tunnel; the report lists its public key.
web-presets-reason-wireguard-kept = kcc copies the captured private key: two routers with one key break the tunnel.
web-presets-reason-excluded = You left this setting out.
web-presets-inputs-passwords-text = These users' password hashes are bound to the source's realm. Type each password; kcc sends it to the router and keeps it encrypted until the run ends.
web-presets-preview-text = The commands kcc sends to the router, in order, with secret values redacted. kcc saves a backup of the router's configuration first and sends them under the fail-safe timer; nothing is saved unless you choose so at the end.
web-presets-count-settings = Settings
web-presets-apply-button = Apply the settings
web-presets-apply-forbidden = Applying is unavailable. Missing permissions: { $missing }. Ask an administrator.
web-presets-apply-confirm-title = Apply the settings to { $router }?
web-presets-apply-confirm-text = kcc saves a backup of the configuration of { $router }, arms its fail-safe timer for { $minutes } minutes and sends the commands. Nothing is saved unless you choose so at the end; if kcc stops reaching the router, the router restores its saved configuration when the timer runs out.
web-presets-apply-busy = Another run is applying to this router. Wait until it finishes.
web-presets-apply-changed = The router changed since the preview, so the plan changed too. Check the plan below and apply again.
web-presets-run-title = Applying the settings
web-presets-run-text = kcc saved a backup of the router's configuration, armed its fail-safe timer and sends the settings one by one. You can leave this page: the run goes on, and coming back shows its progress.
web-presets-applied = The router took every setting and they read back as planned. Keep them unsaved, save them, or roll back.
web-presets-run-interrupted = kcc restarted while it applied the settings. The router restores its saved configuration by itself when its fail-safe timer runs out.
web-presets-failure-cancelled = You stopped the run. Roll back to restore the saved configuration.
web-presets-failure-failed = The run stopped before every setting was verified. Review the result, then roll back.
web-presets-failure-settings = The settings could not be read again. Check the preset, or start the copy again.
web-presets-results-text = Keep unsaved: the router runs the settings until it restarts. Save: the router keeps them after restarts. Roll back: the router returns to the configuration it saved before.
web-presets-keep = Keep unsaved
web-presets-save-router = Save on the router
web-presets-rollback-forbidden = Rolling back needs the Destructive permission. If nobody keeps or saves the settings, the router restores its saved configuration by itself when its fail-safe timer runs out.
web-presets-rollback-title = Roll back the settings on { $router }?
web-presets-rollback-text = kcc restores the configuration { $router } saved before the run; the router may restart. Type the router name to confirm.
web-presets-finish-kept = The settings run on the router unsaved and last until it restarts. Save them on the configuration page to keep them.
web-presets-finish-saved = The settings are saved on the router.
web-presets-finish-rolled-back = The settings are rolled back: the router runs the configuration it had saved before.
web-presets-finish-closed = The run ended without changes to keep on the router.
web-presets-keys-title = New WireGuard public keys
web-presets-keys-text = Register each public key on the VPN server its tunnel connects to.
web-presets-keys-interface = Interface
web-presets-keys-key = Public key
web-presets-keys-kept = The captured private key was copied to { $name }: another router may use the same key.
web-presets-downloads = Download the report
web-presets-group-empty = No setting.
web-explorer-persists-immediately = Takes effect and is saved by the router at once: no save is needed and the fail-safe timer cannot roll it back.
web-segments-col-address = Address
web-segments-col-dhcp = DHCP range
web-segments-col-nat = NAT
web-segments-col-hotspot = New devices allowed
web-segments-col-wifi = Wi-Fi
web-segments-col-ports = Trunk ports
web-segments-col-policy = Connection policy
web-segments-incomplete = Incomplete
web-segments-incomplete-note = An incomplete segment is missing some of the objects kcc created for it. Deleting it removes what is left.
web-segments-missing = Missing
web-segments-empty = No segments yet.
web-segments-scope = Only segments created by kcc are listed; other bridges and VLANs are on the Network page.
web-segments-delete-title = Delete this segment from { $name }?
web-segments-delete-text = Devices connected to this segment lose their network.
web-segments-delete-removed = Deleting segment { $value } removes these router objects and their settings:
web-segments-delete-kept = These ports stay; only VLAN { $value } is taken off them:
web-segments-delete-confirm = Delete segment
web-segments-delete-changed = The segment changed after this dialog opened. Check what goes now and confirm again.
web-segments-delete-gone = The segment is no longer on the router.
web-segments-read-error = The router's segments could not be read.
web-secret-new-password = New password
web-secret-new-key = New key
web-secret-password = Password
web-secret-repeat = Type it again
web-secret-keep-help = Leave both fields empty to keep the current one. kcc never shows it.
web-secret-mismatch = The two entries differ. Type the same value in both fields.
web-secret-unchanged = Nothing was sent: both fields were empty, so the stored value stays.
web-secret-confirm = Nothing was sent. Confirm this change with Apply in its dialog.
web-secret-done = { $what }: the new value was sent, and the router reports a value stored. kcc checks only that it is there, never what it is. The change stays unsaved until you save the configuration.
web-secret-wifi-title = Wi-Fi password: { $name }
web-secret-wifi-intro = Devices join this access point with this password. Each device needs the new one to connect again.
web-secret-wifi-help = 8 to 63 characters. Leave both fields empty to keep the current password.
web-secret-wifi-rule = Use 8 to 63 characters.
web-secret-wan-title = Connection password: { $name }
web-secret-wan-help = The password your provider gave you. Leave both fields empty to keep the current one.
web-secret-user-title = Password of { $name }
web-secret-user-help = Leave both fields empty to keep the current password.
web-secret-user-protected = kcc signs in to the router with this account, so its password is not changed here: a wrong one would cut kcc off. Change it on the router, then enter the new password in kcc with Edit router.
web-secret-add-help = Optional. An account without a password cannot sign in.
web-secret-set-password = Set password
web-secret-set-ipsec = Set IPsec key
web-secret-set-psk = Set pre-shared key
web-secret-set-xauth = Set XAuth password
web-secret-set-account = Set an account's password
web-secret-vpn-password-title = VPN password: { $name }
web-secret-vpn-ipsec-title = IPsec pre-shared key: { $name }
web-secret-vpn-profile-title = Pre-shared key of IPsec profile { $name }
web-secret-vpn-xauth-title = XAuth password of IPsec profile { $name }
web-secret-ike-title = IPsec server pre-shared key
web-secret-ike-intro = Clients of the IPsec/IKEv2 server sign in with this key.
web-secret-ike-name = Key name
web-secret-ike-name-help = The name of the router's IKE key for this server, as the router shows it.
web-secret-ike-name-error = Enter the key's name as the router shows it, without spaces.
web-secret-vpn-account-title = VPN account password
web-secret-vpn-account-intro = A router account signs in to the PPTP/L2TP, SSTP and OpenConnect servers with its password; its tags decide which servers it may use.
web-secret-vpn-no-account = No router account can be changed here. Add one on the router users page.
web-secret-account = Account
web-secret-account-help = The account kcc signs in with is not listed: change its password on the router.
web-secret-peer-help = Optional. Leave it empty to keep the peer's current key; kcc never shows it.
web-secret-import-done = Imported. The keys from the file were sent, and the router reports each one stored; kcc checks only that they are there, never their values. The change stays unsaved until you save the configuration.
web-explorer-confirm-persist-text = The command changes the configuration of { $router }, and the router saves it at once. kcc backs up the saved configuration first.
web-explorer-done-persisted = Command completed. The router stored the change already; no save is needed.
web-explorer-mixed-persistence = Command completed. The router stored these catalog paths at once: { $paths }. The rest is not saved and needs an explicit save.
web-explorer-mixed-persistence-before = The router will store these catalog paths at once: { $paths }. The rest will stay unsaved until you explicitly save it.
web-explorer-partial-persisted = { $succeeded } batch items applied and { $failed } were refused. The successful changes were stored by the router at once; no save is needed.
web-explorer-partial-unsaved = { $succeeded } batch items applied and { $failed } were refused. The successful changes are not saved yet.
web-explorer-confirm-mixed-text = The command will change the configuration of { $router }. kcc will first back up the saved configuration. Some changes will be stored at once; the rest will need an explicit save.
web-vpn-error-psk = Enter a WireGuard preshared key: 44 characters of Base64. Leave the field empty to keep the stored key.
web-explorer-partial-mixed = { $succeeded } batch items applied and { $failed } were refused. The router stored these catalog paths at once: { $paths }. The rest of the successful changes is not saved and needs an explicit save.
web-explorer-partial-answered = { $succeeded } batch items answered and { $failed } were refused.
web-refusal-title = The request was not sent: your role does not allow it on this router.
web-refusal-missing =
    { $count ->
        [one] Missing permission: { $permissions }. An administrator can add it to your role.
       *[other] Missing permissions: { $permissions }. An administrator can add them to your role.
    }
web-refusal-toast = Refused: your role does not allow this on this router. Nothing was changed.
web-migrate-nothing-to-send = Nothing to send: the target already matches.
web-bracket-unowned = This change has to come from a page request; nothing was sent.
web-router-auth-help = Automatic uses the scheme the router offers. An API token replaces the password.
web-router-auth-auto = Automatic (ndw2, ndw4 or HTTP digest)
web-router-auth-ndw2 = ndw2
web-router-auth-ndw4 = ndw4
web-router-auth-digest = HTTP digest
web-router-auth-token = API token
web-router-token = API token
web-router-token-stored = A token is stored. Leave empty to keep it while the address, login and TLS mode stay the same.
web-router-read = Read-only polling account
web-router-read-help = Optional. kcc polls the router's status with this account instead of the management login. Enter the login and password together.
web-router-read-login = Read-only login
web-router-read-password = Read-only password
web-router-read-stored = A read-only password is stored. Leave empty to keep it while the address, login, TLS mode and read-only login stay the same.
web-router-read-remove = Remove read-only login
web-router-error-auth = Choose a sign-in mode from the list.
web-router-error-token = Enter the API token.
web-router-error-read-login = Enter the read-only login for this password.
web-router-error-read-password = Enter the read-only password for this login.
web-time-utc = { $time } UTC
web-router-error-permissions = The credential file of this router can be read by other users. Run chmod 600 on it on the kcc host and try again.
web-wizard-runs-limit = You already have 10 unfinished runs of this wizard. Finish or close one first; a run left unchanged for a day no longer counts.
web-migrate-inputs-password-user = This password field does not belong to this user any more. Reload the page and type the passwords again.
web-dhcp-error-name-taken = A pool with this name already exists. Edit that pool instead.
web-dhcp-error-dns-one = Enter at most one DNS server address.
web-secret-changed = { $what }: the new value was sent, and the router now stores a value different from the one before. kcc checks only that it changed, never what it is, so setting the same value again is reported as not applied. The change stays unsaved until you save the configuration.
